WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.480
It is a very deep

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.720
dive with a lot of repercussions to that
come up too fast.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.960
Bubbles would form inside your blood,
inside your tissues

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.920
and cause ill effects.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.480
To get to 90 meters
you'd be looking at 4 or 5 minutes

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.640
to get down there.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.640
It's very dark because 
you're very deep.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.480
So there's very little light penetration

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.240
and you come down in the dark
and you start to slowly realize

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.440
there's some shape coming up ahead
underneath you.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.440
The atmosphere at the break
when you arrive there is quite spooky.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.760
The very first thing I noticed was
there was a lot of net.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.720
It was basically rope netting,
so very heavy,

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.880
but it does cover everything.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.440
The problem was that

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.320
we were not 100% sure that the

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.080
that the ship is Karlsruhe.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.200
So we decided to go and try and find
the name written on the ship,

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.000
which in a more luxurious ship

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.920
would be bronze or brass
letters riveted into the hull.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.360
As we near the bough,

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.280
the amount of netting seemed 
to increase.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.120
And what you don't want to do as a 
diver is try to get under it

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.840
because that risks you being trapped,

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.120
tangled within it.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:55.720
To be able to uncover the letters,
we had to cut

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:59.360
some of the nets away.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.720
It wasn't easy, but eventually,
once the nets dropped away,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.720
we could finally see what lay beneath.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.680
And what became apparent was that 
the the bridge area

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.720
was heavily damaged.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.480
There's a huge hole in the middle

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.160
of the ship.

